/**
 * The Hermes theme system: one token vocabulary, skins as data.
 *
 * Three tiers share the `--name` namespace so the extension skin protocol and the
 * Tailwind `@theme` map speak the same language:
 * - palette: the colours a skin is made of (`--bg`, `--accent`, `--border`, ...)
 * - semantic: roles derived from the palette (`--accent-fg`, `--link-color`, `--selection-bg`, ...)
 * - component: the few knobs components expose (`--composer-bg`, `--session-active-fg`, ...)
 *
 * `BASE` holds the value of every token for the light scheme plus the dark overrides;
 * each skin overrides a subset in `tokens` (both schemes) and `dark` (dark only), which
 * is exactly the cascade the legacy stylesheet built out of `:root`, `:root.dark`,
 * `:root[data-skin]` and `:root.dark[data-skin]`. No component rule mentions a skin;
 * skins that need a structural variant declare a trait (see `traits`).
 *
 * `renderThemeCss` turns this into the stylesheet the Vite plugin serves as
 * `virtual:hermes-theme.css`; `tailwind.css` maps the same names into utilities.
 */

